Package: obsmage
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3
Recommends: obs-studio
Description: OBS Studio kept as a living, literate configuration (add-on package)
 obsmage wraps the whole OBS configuration in a key/value atom layer so every
 setting can be read, diffed and versioned, with credentials kept out of
 everything published. This package holds the command line tools (omg-atoms,
 omg-compose), the build healer, and the obsmage-core plugin for an OBS Studio
 installed from the distribution.
 .
 It touches nothing outside /usr and has no configuration files, so removing it
 removes all of it. It never writes your OBS files unless you ask.
